  "response_text": "The body of water is the **Black Sea**.\n\nThe name \"Euxine\" comes from the Ancient Greek *Euxeinos* (\u0395\u1f54\u03be\u03b5\u03b9\u03bd\u03bf\u03c2), meaning \"hospitable.\" This was a name given by early Greek colonists who found the coastal regions welcoming and conducive to settlement. (This stands in contrast to its later name, the *Pontus Euxinus*, and the more ominous \"Axeinos,\" meaning \"inhospitable,\" which was sometimes used due to the perceived dangers of the sea).",
